ould separate me from my kid he said  as for fernanda she said that they  treated her bad and  scolded her how do you feel when you  hear that  powerless  a report issued by the health and human  services department actually shows that  children separated  from their parents at the border were  more likely to have higher levels of  fear abandonment post-traumatic stress  and likely to consider self-harm or even  suicide and gail we have spoken with a  number of these families and their  children they say there are some big  psychological impacts  that they will be dealing with for a  very long time gail  ray this is heartbreaking we went to  texas at the time  matter of fact saw you there too we saw  those people  with their families were there some bad  eggs in the group maybe  but that's not what we saw what we saw  were desperate people  trying to come here for a better life  for their children and for themselves  and to protect their children i can't  understand why there wasn't a system in  place  to keep track of the kids once they were  separated from their parents we wouldn't  stand for this  if somebody did this to american  children we would not stand for this  do you have do you happen to know how  the system worked  you know gail i think a lot of this  happened because the policy was  implemented so  quickly that the administration couldn't  coordinate properly with all the federal  agencies that were involved  we were talking about nearly a dozen of  them that were impacted from border  patrol dhs to the department of  health and human services that we just  talked about right now so i think the  coordination  was a very very big issue people were  just caught off guard  and they didn't know and didn't have a  tracking system in place it's  heartbreaking it should be all hands on  deck to straighten this out thank you  very much maria thank you very much
 

